In Spring Boot, by default your app runs on port 8080.
If you want your application to run on a dynamic/random port, you have a few options:

1. Random Port via application.properties
server.port=0


Setting server.port=0 tells Spring Boot to pick a free random port at startup.

Useful for integration tests or when running multiple instances of the same service.

2. Programmatically Set Port

You can set the port dynamically based on logic (e.g., from DB, config service, or env variable):

import org.springframework.boot.web.server.WebServerFactoryCustomizer;
import org.springframework.boot.web.embedded.tomcat.TomcatServletWebServerFactory;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class CustomPortConfig implements WebServerFactoryCustomizer<TomcatServletWebServerFactory> {

    @Override
    public void customize(TomcatServletWebServerFactory factory) {
        int dynamicPort = 9090; // fetch from config, env, or generate dynamically
        factory.setPort(dynamicPort);
    }
}

3. Using Command Line Argument

When running the jar:

java -jar myapp.jar --server.port=9091


Or:

java -jar myapp.jar --server.port=0   # dynamic random port

4. Accessing the Assigned Dynamic Port

If you used server.port=0, you may need to retrieve the actual port:

import org.springframework.boot.web.context.WebServerApplicationContext;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

import jakarta.annotation.PostConstruct;

@Component
public class PortLogger {

    private final WebServerApplicationContext serverAppContext;

    public PortLogger(WebServerApplicationContext serverAppContext) {
        this.serverAppContext = serverAppContext;
    }

    @PostConstruct
    public void logPort() {
        int port = serverAppContext.getWebServer().getPort();
        System.out.println("Application started on dynamic port: " + port);
    }
}


✅ Summary:

server.port=0 → random dynamic port.

Customizer → set programmatically.

CLI args → override per run.

Use WebServerApplicationContext to read the assigned port at runtime.